# Named again so that these lines survive if the catch-all above is ever narrowed or delegated. Each one can
# switch off or rewrite the checks themselves, so a change to it needs the owner's review, not only a green CI:
# - .wormsign-baseline.json suppresses findings. A new entry silences a finding in every scan of main after merge
#   (wormsign diff reads the baseline from the base branch, so it cannot silence the pull request that adds it).
# - .github/ holds the workflows, which run with repository tokens and run wormsign's own gate, plus this file.
#   A workflow change can weaken the gate, widen permissions or swap a pinned action.
# - data/iocs/ is what every user's scan matches against, and what update-iocs serves from main. A removed or
#   wrong entry hides a compromise for everyone.
# - THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md is the attribution the Apache-2.0 IOC data requires; it must change with data/iocs/.
# - action.yml is what other repositories run when they use this Action; its inputs and steps run in their CI.
# - src/vendor/ is third-party code that runs inside wormsign (the vendored TOML parser). It must stay
#   byte-identical to the pinned npm tarball (src/vendor/smol-toml/VENDORED.json, scripts/verify-vendor.mjs).
/.wormsign-baseline.json  @stgllghr
/.github/                 @stgllghr
/data/iocs/               @stgllghr
/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md   @stgllghr
/action.yml               @stgllghr
/src/vendor/              @stgllghr
